OK    LOWRANK_M256_s1

============================================================
  C06 depth 4 complete.

  READ IT WITH:
    python -m scripts.sweep_report out/c06_head_lowrank/d4

  THE COMPARISON IS HORIZONTAL, AT MATCHED COST. At V=32768 and d=256:
    LOWRANK_M16  ~ MON_M1024_m1_8   (3.07e7 vs 3.07e7)
    LOWRANK_M18  ~ MON_M256         (3.11e7 vs 3.11e7)
    LOWRANK_M40  ~ MON_M1024        (3.55e7 vs 3.55e7)
  Those pairs are the whole sweep. Everything else fills the curves.

  THE DECISION RULE, FIXED BEFORE THE RUN: MON_M1024 scored 1.2559 in c05.
  If LOWRANK_M40 reaches 1.2559 or better, the block-diagonal structure
  buys nothing a plain rank reduction does not, and the direction is over.
  Only if LOWRANK_M40 is clearly worse is the depth ladder (Q10) worth it.

  WATCH THE WALL CLOCK, NOT ONLY THE FLOPS. A learned Phi is one dense
  matmul and runs at tensor-core speed; Monarch is two smaller ones plus a
  transpose. c05 measured Monarch at 0.762x dense time against learned_W's
  0.968x, so Monarch's advantage there was larger than its FLOPs advantage.
  If that inverts at small M the FLOPs axis is the wrong one to argue on.
